# Order of two tasks of equal priority due at the same step.
# Implementation-defined: ed.3 6.8.2 ranks ready tasks by priority and
# says nothing about ties. marks reads 12 when A ran first, 21 when B did.
# IronPLC cannot run two program instances (ironplc#1613), so the records
# are what matiec does: declaration order, A then B, every step.
period_ms: 100
inputs:
outputs: marks
status: implementation-defined
reference: IEC 61131-3 ed.3 6.8.2 (TASK PRIORITY; ties not specified)
---
0 => marks=12
1 => marks=1212
2 => marks=121212
3 => marks=12121212
4 => marks=1212121212
